---
import '../../../styles/finger-atlas-v4.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" /><meta name="description" content="A continuous, multiscale anatomical model of individual finger sensory and motor pathways." /><title>Finger Pathway Atlas V4 · Build the Simulation</title></head>
  <body>
    <main id="atlas-v4">
      <header class="atlas-top"><div><span class="atlas-edition">BUILD THE SIMULATION · ANATOMICAL EDITION IV</span><h1>Finger Pathway Atlas</h1></div><div class="top-actions"><a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/v3/" target="_top">V3 original</a><a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/references/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reference plates ↗</a><button id="help-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="help-panel">About / controls</button><button id="fullscreen" aria-label="Enter full screen">⛶</button></div></header>
      <div class="atlas-workspace">
        <aside class="atlas-sidebar" aria-label="Explore anatomy">
          <div class="sidebar-title"><span>01 / EXPLORE</span><button id="overview">Whole anatomy</button></div>
          <nav id="region-list" aria-label="Anatomical regions"></nav>
          <section class="route-controls"><span class="eyebrow">02 / FOLLOW A PATHWAY</span><label for="route-kind">Pathway family</label><select id="route-kind"><option value="touch">Touch</option><option value="pain">Free endings / pain</option><option value="proprioception">Proprioception</option><option value="motor">Motor</option></select><label for="route-select">Individual modeled route</label><select id="route-select"></select><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="isolate" /> Isolate this route</label><div class="paired"><button id="previous">← Previous</button><button id="next">Next stop →</button></div></section>
          <details class="display-controls"><summary>Display & performance</summary><label for="quality">Detail budget</label><select id="quality"><option value="balanced">Balanced</option><option value="light">Light</option><option value="high">High detail</option></select><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="skin" checked /> Holographic skin</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="envelopes" checked /> Anatomical surfaces</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="supports" checked /> Cell support membranes</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="labels" checked /> Region labels</label><label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="myelin" checked /> Myelin at close range</label><button id="export-map">Export cells & source map</button></details>
          <p class="sidebar-note">One spatial model. Every modeled cell keeps its identity as you move between scales.</p>
        </aside>
        <section class="atlas-stage" id="stage" aria-label="3D anatomical model">
          <canvas id="viewport" aria-label="Interactive 3D model. Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom, right-drag to pan." tabindex="0"></canvas>
          <div class="view-heading"><span id="view-eyebrow">CONTINUOUS ANATOMY / MILLIMETERS</span><h2 id="view-title">From fingertip to cortex</h2><p id="view-description">Intact anatomy, individually identified cells, connected pathways.</p><button id="inspect-region" class="inspect-region">Open V3 cell detail ↗</button></div>
          <div id="region-labels"></div>
          <div id="load-state" role="status"><span class="loading-dot"></span><span id="load-text">Preparing individual pathways…</span></div>
          <div id="fatal-error" role="alert" hidden><h2>The 3D viewer could not open</h2><p id="error-message"></p><button id="retry">Try again</button><a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/references/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the reference plates</a></div>
          <section class="cell-inspector" id="inspector" aria-label="Selected pathway">
            <div class="inspector-title"><span id="route-tag">MODELED TOUCH ROUTE</span><button id="clear-selection">Clear highlight</button><button id="inspector-toggle" aria-expanded="true">Collapse</button></div>
            <h3 id="route-title"></h3><div id="route-stops" aria-label="Pathway stops"></div>
            <div class="cell-row"><label for="cell-select">Cell identity</label><select id="cell-select"></select><button id="focus-cell">Inspect cell</button><button id="focus-ending">Inspect ending</button></div>
            <p id="cell-description"></p><p class="connection-note" id="connection-note"></p>
          </section>
          <footer class="scene-footer"><span id="scene-stats" role="status"></span><span id="scale-bar"><i></i><span></span></span><span class="gesture-hint">Drag · orbit &nbsp; Scroll · zoom &nbsp; Right-drag · pan</span></footer>
        </section>
      </div>
      <section id="help-panel" class="help-panel" hidden aria-label="About this model"><button id="help-close" aria-label="Close help">×</button><span class="eyebrow">VERSION 4 / MODEL SCOPE</span><h2>A complete route for every modeled cell.</h2><p>Choose a region, then use <strong>Inspect cell</strong> or <strong>Inspect ending</strong> to move from anatomy to cellular detail. Scroll back out to see where that same cell belongs. Next stop follows the selected route through its relay cells.</p><p>V4 integrates V3’s detailed cell models and all retained noncortical anatomical surfaces into one millimeter coordinate system. Original membrane meshes load near the camera; distant cells retain their paths and identities. Detail budgets limit the number of visible objects, preserving the source geometry of each inspected model. Overview fibers have a minimum screen width for readability. Use Cell support membranes to show or hide whole support structures around an ending. The scale bar measures the view plane through the camera target.</p><p>The cortical endpoint is intentionally limited to the two gyri used by this finger pathway: left precentral primary motor cortex (M1) and left postcentral primary somatosensory cortex (S1). Selecting <strong>M1 + S1 coronal cortex</strong> opens paired coronal-orientation cut faces so both gyri and both six-layer cross-sections remain visible together. M1 uses an agranular prior with a very thin layer IV and expanded layer V; S1 uses a granular prior with a prominent layer IV.</p><p>H01 guides cellular morphology, neuropil, glia, vessels and close-range visual density, but H01 is temporal cortex—not a measured M1 or S1 connectome. BigBrain supplies region-specific six-layer and thickness priors. DKI references guide probabilistic corticofugal, thalamocortical and short association orientation envelopes; they do not identify individual axons, synapses or exact endpoints. Open the <a href="/assets/finger-pathway-atlas/v4/cortex-sources.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cortex source record</a> for the implementation boundary and citations.</p><p>This is a representative, constructed circuit, <strong>not a complete biological census or an experimentally traced human connectome</strong>. Each synaptic relay is a different neuron. Sensory cells have a dorsal-root-ganglion soma; motor output bypasses that ganglion. Free-ending pathways cross in the spinal cord; touch and motor pathways cross separately in the medulla.</p><p>Histology and electron microscopy in the supplied comparison packet guide cell shapes, support cells, and endings. Those images span different species and tissues; they do not supply matched end-to-end reconstructions. V3’s measured human light-microscopy cortical traces remain attached to route identities, while the new paired M1/S1 tissue volume supplies their regional context. No electrical activity or biomechanical response is simulated.</p><p>Source anatomy: BodyParts3D / Anatomography, Database Center for Life Science, CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan; light overview surfaces with original V3 mesh detail loaded nearby. See the <a href="/assets/finger-pathway-atlas/v4/provenance.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">V4 source record</a> and <a href="/simulations/finger-pathway-atlas/references/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">50 comparison plates</a>. Plate model panels show V3 and are retained as the development baseline.</p><p class="help-keys">Keyboard: <kbd>Home</kbd> whole anatomy · <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd> pathway stops · <kbd>Escape</kbd> close this panel. Touch: one finger orbit, two fingers zoom/pan.</p></section>
      <div id="toast" role="status" hidden></div>
    </main>
    <script>
      import { installSensorimotorCortex } from '../../../lib/finger-atlas-v4/sensorimotor-cortex.mjs';
      installSensorimotorCortex();
      import('../../../lib/finger-atlas-v4/viewer.js');
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
